{{also|f@|F.|f|F|ḟ|Ḟ|.f|Appendix:Variations of “f”}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{sense|and the following}} From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|folio||on the (next) page}}, ablative of {{m|la|folium||leaf, page}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|grammar}} {{abbreviation of|feminine|lang=en}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} {{abbreviation of|form|lang=en}} {{non-gloss definition|Used in certain three-part names}}
# and the following (page, paragraph, etc.)

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|and the following}} When used, {{m|en||f.}} has no space between it and the preceding number and is followed by a period. If more than one following section is meant, {{m|en|ff.}} is used.
: For example, “Hornblower 258f.” would refer to pages 258–259 while “Hornblower 258ff.” would refer to an undetermined number of pages following page 258; more casually “258–” (no end specified).

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|et seq.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|ff.}}

